  "before_edn": "{:db/id 17592186087717 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186087518 :question/id #uuid \"53ce2176-ae44-578d-8fba-35c5018d4162\" :question/math-academy-id \"e-5075\" :question/problem \"For the parametric curve\\n\\n$$\\nx=3t, \\\\,\\\\,\\\\, y=t^3, \\\\quad -3\\\\leq t \\\\leq 3,\\n$$\\n\\nfill in the following table of values.\\n\\n\\n\\n<div class=\\\"source-table-scroll\\\"><table class=\\\"source-table\\\" data-rules=\\\"all\\\" data-table-align=\\\"center\\\" data-frame=\\\"true\\\">\\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\\\"true\\\">\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\" data-fill=\\\"#D6EAF8\\\"><strong>$t$</strong></td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$-3$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$-2$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$-1$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$0$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$1$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$2$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$3$</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr data-next-row=\\\"true\\\">\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\" data-fill=\\\"#D6EAF8\\\">$x$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\"></td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\"></td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\"></td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\"></td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\"></td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\"></td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\"></td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\" data-fill=\\\"#D6EAF8\\\">$y$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\"></td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\"></td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\"></td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\"></td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\"></td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\"></td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\"></td>\\n</tr>\\n</tbody></table></div>\\n\\n\" :question/worked-solution \"First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x=3t.$ This gives\\n\\n\\n\\n<div class=\\\"source-table-scroll\\\"><table class=\\\"source-table\\\" data-rules=\\\"all\\\" data-table-align=\\\"center\\\" data-frame=\\\"true\\\">\\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\\\"true\\\">\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\" data-fill=\\\"#D6EAF8\\\"><strong>$t$</strong></td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$-3$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$-2$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$-1$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$0$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$1$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$2$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$3$</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr data-next-row=\\\"true\\\">\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\" data-fill=\\\"#D6EAF8\\\">$x$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$-9$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$-6$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$-3$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$0$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$3$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$6$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$9$</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\" data-fill=\\\"#D6EAF8\\\">$y$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\"></td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\"></td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\"></td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\"></td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\"></td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\"></td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\"></td>\\n</tr>\\n</tbody></table></div>\\n\\n\\nNow, we work out the $y$-values using $y=t^3.$ This gives\\n\\n\\n\\n<div class=\\\"source-table-scroll\\\"><table class=\\\"source-table\\\" data-rules=\\\"all\\\" data-table-align=\\\"center\\\" data-frame=\\\"true\\\">\\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\\\"true\\\">\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\" data-fill=\\\"#D6EAF8\\\"><strong>$t$</strong></td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$-3$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$-2$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$-1$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$0$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$1$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$2$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$3$</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr data-next-row=\\\"true\\\">\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\" data-fill=\\\"#D6EAF8\\\">$x$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$-9$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$-6$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$-3$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$0$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$3$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$6$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$9$</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\" data-fill=\\\"#D6EAF8\\\">$y$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$-27$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$-8$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$-1$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$0$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$1$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$8$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$27$</td>\\n</tr>\\n</tbody></table></div>\\n\\n\"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid \"bbf50e27-a8c3-52e7-be21-5d7ed61e5512\" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186050790 :topic/id #uuid \"6734489a-e850-531c-afa4-62b5b9a5d87f\" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id 17592186054676} {:db/id 17592186054694} {:db/id 17592186054695} {:db/id 17592186054802}] :topic/math-academy-id 95 :topic/next [{:db/id 17592186048678} {:db/id 17592186050103} {:db/id 17592186050763}] :topic/title \"Graphing Linear Equations\"}] :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id 17592186698142 :question-generator/id #uuid \"b80586aa-f033-54d0-9892-52ba7d05c425\" :question-generator/script \"generators/e9/e98534e6f6a579edf98679ec13ed814bd5b36b5878707aaae86b7a338c3a83da/generator.py\"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186088269 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"c5c9c6f1-88a9-5814-8d7f-824388fe769d\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-15\" :db/id 17592186086269} {:answer/id #uuid \"c95ef482-a715-5d27-8322-272d06aefa28\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-10\" :db/id 17592186086270} {:answer/id #uuid \"dd13ebf0-fcc4-5780-a2ef-c58a92669901\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"9\" :db/id 17592186086271} {:answer/id #uuid \"3ae5b9a5-e0be-5b47-b2de-3e04a707aebe\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"14\" :db/id 17592186086272} {:answer/id #uuid \"70b93ffd-0a6c-5e4b-a149-c7a58e10d173\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"12\" :db/id 17592186086273}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"3ae5b9a5-e0be-5b47-b2de-3e04a707aebe\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"14\" :db/id 17592186086272} :answer-field/id #uuid \"155c89c2-1972-5fdf-8d50-c32635afc935\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186086268}] :question/id #uuid \"5cc3bc31-0264-5908-8539-6e444261bf21\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-6827\" :question/problem \"For the parametric curve\\n$$\\n\\\\displaystyle x = t^{2} + t, y = t^{2} - t,-4 \\\\le t \\\\le 4,\\n$$\\nconsider the following table of values:\\n\\n\\n\\n<div class=\\\"source-table-scroll\\\"><table class=\\\"source-table\\\" data-rules=\\\"all\\\" data-table-align=\\\"center\\\" data-frame=\\\"true\\\">\\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\\\"true\\\">\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\" data-fill=\\\"#D6EAF8\\\"><strong>$t$</strong></td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$-4$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$-2$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$-1$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$0$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$1$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$3$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$4$</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr data-next-row=\\\"true\\\">\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\" data-fill=\\\"#D6EAF8\\\">$x$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$12$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$a$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$0$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$0$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$2$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$c$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$20$</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\" data-fill=\\\"#D6EAF8\\\">$y$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$20$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$6$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$2$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$b$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$0$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$6$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$12$</td>\\n</tr>\\n</tbody></table></div>\\n\\n\\nFind the value of $a + b + c$.\" :question/worked-solution \"Substitute the indicated parameter values: $a=(-2)^2+(-2)=2$, $b=0^2-0=0$, and $c=3^2+3=12$. Thus $a+b+c=14$.\"} {:db/id 17592186088270 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"3c987a4c-ef82-50f8-9c2f-24369b52299f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-5\" :db/id 17592186333562} {:answer/id #uuid \"448c0861-60dc-5277-abf0-6324c4313b9c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-6\" :db/id 17592186333623} {:answer/id #uuid \"4ec62518-f2da-54a6-b78e-7803c2af25ea\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3\" :db/id 17592186333712} {:answer/id #uuid \"4f618bb1-1a30-5478-b04d-5d8c290174ad\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-2\" :db/id 17592186333716} {:answer/id #uuid \"cc14822b-2861-53db-8d57-7b85cd391a64\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4\" :db/id 17592186334768}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"3c987a4c-ef82-50f8-9c2f-24369b52299f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-5\" :db/id 17592186333562} :answer-field/id #uuid \"e19de855-513e-569d-b86d-f599dde05f25\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186335632}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"2efd117e-aa4e-5314-8b1b-8bd86f2a35c1\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-6834\" :question/problem \"For the parametric curve\\n\\n$$\\nx={t}^{2}-4,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,y=\\\\frac{5}{2}-\\\\frac{t}{2},\\\\,-1\\\\le t\\\\le 5,\\n$$\\n\\nconsider the following table of values:\\n\\n\\n\\n<div class=\\\"source-table-scroll\\\"><table class=\\\"source-table\\\" data-rules=\\\"all\\\" data-table-align=\\\"center\\\" data-frame=\\\"true\\\">\\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\\\"true\\\">\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\" data-fill=\\\"#D6EAF8\\\"><strong>$t$</strong></td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$-1$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$0$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$1$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$2$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$3$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$4$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$5$</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr data-next-row=\\\"true\\\">\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\" data-fill=\\\"#D6EAF8\\\">$x$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">${\\\\color{blue}a}$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$-4$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$-3$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$0$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$5$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$12$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$21$</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\" data-fill=\\\"#D6EAF8\\\">$y$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$3$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$\\\\frac{5}{2}$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">${\\\\color{blue}b}$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$\\\\frac{3}{2}$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$1$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">$\\\\frac{1}{2}$</td>\\n<td data-cell-align=\\\"center\\\">${\\\\color{blue}c}$</td>\\n</tr>\\n</tbody></table></div>\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nFind the value of $a-b+c.$\" :question/worked-solution \"- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=-1$ into $x={t}^{2}-4.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\na=(-1)^{2}-4=1-4=-3.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=1$ into $y=\\\\frac{5}{2}-\\\\frac{t}{2}.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nb=\\\\frac{5}{2}-\\\\frac{1}{2}=\\\\frac{4}{2}=2.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=5$ into $y=\\\\frac{5}{2}-\\\\frac{t}{2}.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nc=\\\\frac{5}{2}-\\\\frac{5}{2}=0.\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, we have\\n\\n$$\\na-b+c=-3-2+0=-5.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186233325 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"023f3e70-1c18-56f9-a0dc-bbd6d23f44df\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-123754\" :question/problem \"For the parametric curve\\n\\n$$\\nx=t-4,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,y=1-2{t}^{2},\\\\,0\\\\le t\\\\le 4,\\n$$\\n\\nconsider the following table of values:\\n\\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $a$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\\n| $y$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $b$ | $c$ | $-31$ |\\n\\n\\n\\nFind the value of $a+b+c.$\" :question/worked-solution \"- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=0$ into $x=t-4.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\na=0-4=-4.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=2$ into $y=1-2{t}^{2}.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nb=1-2(2)^{2}=-7.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=3$ into $y=1-2{t}^{2}.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nc=1-2(3)^{2}=-17\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, we have\\n\\n$$\\na+b+c=-4+(-7)+(-17)=-28.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186233831 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"d258e642-b9a6-5bf1-b482-5f152ab7aaad\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"7\" :db/id 17592186232635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"d258e642-b9a6-5bf1-b482-5f152ab7aaad\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"7\" :db/id 17592186232635} :answer-field/id #uuid \"52f71c9c-2f6b-5370-8a49-95e60baaf004\" :answer-field/key \"field-1\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186232634} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"49847da4-c519-552f-850e-48e4275cefef\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"213\" :db/id 17592186232637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"49847da4-c519-552f-850e-48e4275cefef\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"213\" :db/id 17592186232637} :answer-field/id #uuid \"415b1ff5-fd3e-5864-b71e-dcccb0c3c658\" :answer-field/key \"field-2\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186232636} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"b3cfa260-48a2-5cf6-94ef-725c7428f7f1\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-8\" :db/id 17592186232639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"b3cfa260-48a2-5cf6-94ef-725c7428f7f1\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-8\" :db/id 17592186232639} :answer-field/id #uuid \"858a5c87-649c-59d5-a39d-60ba696bb7d6\" :answer-field/key \"field-3\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186232638}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"16325e3c-ebce-5185-863e-0d84f168aa37\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-326248\" :question/problem \"Consider the curve with parametric equations\\n\\n$$\\nx={t}^{3}-\\\\frac{1}{2}t,\\\\,y=1-{t}^{2},\\\\,1\\\\le t\\\\le 6.\\n$$\\n\\nFill in the blanks in the following table of values:\\n\\n| **$t$** | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $\\\\frac{1}{2}$ | {{field-1}} | $\\\\frac{51}{2}$ | $62$ | $\\\\frac{245}{2}$ | {{field-2}} |\\n| $y$ | $0$ | $-3$ | {{field-3}} | $-15$ | $-24$ | $-35$ |\" :question/worked-solution \"- To find the value of $x(2),$ we substitute $t=2$ into $x={t}^{3}-\\\\frac{1}{2}t.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nx(2)=(2)^{3}-\\\\frac{1}{2}(2)=8-1=7.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $y(3),$ we substitute $t=3$ into $y=1-{t}^{2}.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\ny(3)=1-(3)^{2}=1-9=-8.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $x(6),$ we substitute $t=6$ into $x={t}^{3}-\\\\frac{1}{2}t.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nx(6)=(6)^{3}-\\\\frac{1}{2}(6)=216-3=213.\\n$$\\n\\nThen the table is \\n\\n| **$t$** | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $\\\\frac{1}{2}$ | $7$ | $\\\\frac{51}{2}$ | $62$ | $\\\\frac{245}{2}$ | $213$ |\\n| $y$ | $0$ | $-3$ | $-8$ | $-15$ | $-24$ | $-35$ |\"} {:db/id 17592186234248 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"280e1cee-68f8-59f3-a023-f6dd1f086b41\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-2\" :db/id 17592186333358} {:answer/id #uuid \"c16fb7f6-a00e-595d-a28e-2f0a7397869c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"0\" :db/id 17592186334666} {:answer/id #uuid \"d02e3a07-a9eb-5ee2-9205-057f65384e6c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"1\" :db/id 17592186334807} {:answer/id #uuid \"e4417143-3102-5cc2-b8d4-db87db4085b3\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-1\" :db/id 17592186334978} {:answer/id #uuid \"eacbc418-3efa-5b4c-a585-26704419f165\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3\" :db/id 17592186335043}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"e4417143-3102-5cc2-b8d4-db87db4085b3\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-1\" :db/id 17592186334978} :answer-field/id #uuid \"0b5f293a-3b57-563b-b236-87b7649c6cbf\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186335256}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"e3d07c4f-77fc-5e25-9502-ae72735f0f26\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-6832\" :question/problem \"For the parametric curve\\n\\n$$\\nx=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi t}{2}\\\\right),\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,y=\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi t}{3}\\\\right),\\\\,-3\\\\le t\\\\le 3,\\n$$\\n\\nconsider the following table of values:\\n\\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $1$ | $0$ | ${\\\\color{blue}b}$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | ${\\\\color{blue}c}$ |\\n| $y$ | ${\\\\color{blue}a}$ | $-\\\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $\\\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-\\\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-1$ |\\n\\n\\n\\nFind the value of $-a+b+c.$\" :question/worked-solution \"- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=-3$ into $y=\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi t}{3}\\\\right).$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\na=\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi (-3)}{3}\\\\right)=\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\\\pi )=-1.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=-1$ into $y=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi t}{2}\\\\right).$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nb=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi (-1)}{2}\\\\right)=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(-\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{2}\\\\right)=-1.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=3$ into $y=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi t}{2}\\\\right).$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nc=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi (3)}{2}\\\\right)=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{3\\\\pi }{2}\\\\right)=-1.\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, we have\\n\\n$$\\n-a+b+c=-(-1)+(-1)+(-1)=-1.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186234256 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"28dfeac9-12f2-53c4-b4b0-03e187c89f74\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-69923\" :question/problem \"For the parametric curve\\n\\n$$\\nx=-3t,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,y=2t,\\\\,-5\\\\le t\\\\le 0,\\n$$\\n\\nconsider the following table of values:\\n\\n| **$t$** | $-5$ | $-4$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $15$ | $12$ | $9$ | $6$ | $3$ | $c$ |\\n| $y$ | $-10$ | $a$ | $-6$ | $b$ | $-2$ | $0$ |\\n\\n\\n\\nFind the value of $a-b+c.$\" :question/worked-solution \"- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=-4$ into $y=2t.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\na=2(-4)=-8.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=-2$ into $y=2t.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nb=2(-2)-4.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=0$ into $x=-3t.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nc=-3(0)=0.\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, we have\\n\\n$$\\na-b+c=-8-(-4)+0=-4.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186259554 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"3260f191-357e-5fd6-b3f9-51c178134db5\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-4\" :db/id 17592186257221} {:answer/id #uuid \"6d128ce0-efb8-56e1-8023-f299f3be850c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\" :db/id 17592186257742} {:answer/id #uuid \"b18c0515-7610-54e6-b101-c84deb16e608\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-1\" :db/id 17592186258326} {:answer/id #uuid \"f075feb5-f3f8-5129-a941-46db050b2214\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"0\" :db/id 17592186258873} {:answer/id #uuid \"f211cf5f-df49-5a9e-9bde-8f90da57b9b2\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3\" :db/id 17592186258888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"b18c0515-7610-54e6-b101-c84deb16e608\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-1\" :db/id 17592186258326} :answer-field/id #uuid \"7b2b0b8a-76aa-5a6d-9974-c88122a91939\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186259240}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"3cac2494-d877-5849-8ad0-9d49fb79c7df\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-123753\" :question/problem \"For the parametric curve\\n\\n$$\\nx=1-{t}^{2},\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,y=3t+2,\\\\,-2\\\\le t\\\\le 2,\\n$$\\n\\nconsider the following table of values:\\n\\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $-3$ | ${\\\\color{blue}a}$ | $1$ | $0$ | ${\\\\color{blue}c}$ |\\n| $y$ | $-4$ | $-1$ | ${\\\\color{blue}b}$ | $5$ | $8$ |\\n\\n\\n\\nFind the value of $a+b+c.$\" :question/worked-solution \"- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=-1$ into $x=1-{t}^{2}.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\na=1-(-1)^{2}=0.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=0$ into $y=3t+2.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nb=3(0)+2=2.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=2$ into $x=1-{t}^{2}.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nc=1-(2)^{2}=-3.\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, we have\\n\\n$$\\na+b+c=0+2+(-3)=-1.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186259555 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"04f211ed-ddd7-5784-b0dc-35bcae2cefaa\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-5\" :db/id 17592186256825} {:answer/id #uuid \"2de8af09-195f-5b8c-bab0-ef80dd63e84b\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\" :db/id 17592186257188} {:answer/id #uuid \"43228c86-2dad-5bf2-9955-abab71f85368\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-2\" :db/id 17592186257373} {:answer/id #uuid \"7b84009a-c3a3-57ac-ba2b-c913c4990eb7\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-3\" :db/id 17592186257875} {:answer/id #uuid \"8153caf4-964a-58e3-bef6-6c7992bf2466\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"1\" :db/id 17592186257931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"04f211ed-ddd7-5784-b0dc-35bcae2cefaa\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-5\" :db/id 17592186256825} :answer-field/id #uuid \"7d2fb483-072d-5aac-a385-71833c68e6fd\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186259245}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"04aa985e-d3c5-5600-ac7a-83a47e2753a8\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-123755\" :question/problem \"For the parametric curve\\n\\n$$\\nx=4t,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,y=-{t}^{3},\\\\,-3\\\\le t\\\\le 1,\\n$$\\n\\nconsider the following table of values:\\n\\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $-12$ | $-8$ | ${\\\\color{blue}a}$ | ${\\\\color{blue}b}$ | $4$ |\\n| $y$ | $27$ | $8$ | $1$ | $0$ | ${\\\\color{blue}c}$ |\\n\\n\\n\\nFind the value of $a+b+c.$\" :question/worked-solution \"- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=-1$ into $x=4t.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\na=4(-1)=-4.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=0$ into $x=4t.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nb=4(0)=0.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=1$ into $y=-{t}^{3}.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nc=-(1)^{3}=-1.\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, we have\\n\\n$$\\na+b+c=-4+0+(-1)=-5.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186302269 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"bf11f1c2-7e84-52d0-82eb-f0bec75d951c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{1}{2}\" :db/id 17592186300917}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"bf11f1c2-7e84-52d0-82eb-f0bec75d951c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{1}{2}\" :db/id 17592186300917} :answer-field/id #uuid \"909ca647-782d-5026-97c2-4f69d2dbc2de\" :answer-field/key \"field-1\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186301688} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"ca352a99-e4be-5a50-b2d8-376ac2cbd696\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{13}{4}\" :db/id 17592186300970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"ca352a99-e4be-5a50-b2d8-376ac2cbd696\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{13}{4}\" :db/id 17592186300970} :answer-field/id #uuid \"be23546a-6789-50c1-b0de-9f43e3206e3b\" :answer-field/key \"field-3\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186301847} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"315f9757-1b3f-500e-b71c-be24341277dc\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{11}{2}\" :db/id 17592186300203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"315f9757-1b3f-500e-b71c-be24341277dc\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{11}{2}\" :db/id 17592186300203} :answer-field/id #uuid \"cdc547cb-e485-57de-acc6-c64ddfd515ba\" :answer-field/key \"field-2\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186301887}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"97abe29c-aa1a-5961-b330-faf07c8841b1\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-326242\" :question/problem \"Consider the curve with parametric equations\\n\\n$$\\nx=\\\\frac{3}{2}t+1,\\\\,y=-\\\\frac{5}{4}t+2,\\\\,-1\\\\le t\\\\le 4.\\n$$\\n\\nFill in the blanks in the following table of values:\\n\\n| **$t$** | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | {{field-1}} | $1$ | $\\\\frac{5}{2}$ | $4$ | {{field-2}} | $7$ |\\n| $y$ | {{field-3}} | $2$ | $\\\\frac{3}{4}$ | $-\\\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-\\\\frac{7}{4}$ | $-3$ |\" :question/worked-solution \"- To find the value of $x(-1),$ we substitute $t=-1$ into $x=\\\\frac{3}{2}t+1.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nx(-1)=\\\\frac{3}{2}(-1)+1=-\\\\frac{3}{2}+\\\\frac{2}{2}=-\\\\frac{1}{2}.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $y(-1),$ we substitute $t=-1$ into $y=-\\\\frac{5}{4}t+2.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\ny(-1)=-\\\\frac{5}{4}(-1)+2=\\\\frac{5}{4}+\\\\frac{8}{4}=\\\\frac{13}{4}.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $x(3),$ we substitute $t=3$ into $x=\\\\frac{3}{2}t+1.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nx(2)=\\\\frac{3}{2}(3)+1=\\\\frac{9}{2}+\\\\frac{2}{2}=\\\\frac{11}{2}.\\n$$\\n\\nThen the table is \\n\\n \\n\\n| **$t$** | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $-\\\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $\\\\frac{5}{2}$ | $4$ | $\\\\frac{11}{2}$ | $7$ |\\n| $y$ | $\\\\frac{13}{4}$ | $2$ | $\\\\frac{3}{4}$ | $-\\\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-\\\\frac{7}{4}$ | $-3$ |\"} {:db/id 17592186302270 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"43263775-6a23-5d97-906a-a6f79d7a0456\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{9}{2}\" :db/id 17592186300292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"43263775-6a23-5d97-906a-a6f79d7a0456\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{9}{2}\" :db/id 17592186300292} :answer-field/id #uuid \"32519836-bf08-5075-8849-e308dea3e240\" :answer-field/key \"field-3\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186301387} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"2d011c6c-58a6-561f-ae10-6109748dcac4\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"115\" :db/id 17592186300180}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"2d011c6c-58a6-561f-ae10-6109748dcac4\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"115\" :db/id 17592186300180} :answer-field/id #uuid \"57c14b01-f4ee-5c68-bf97-0b1dcdace2d4\" :answer-field/key \"field-2\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186301512} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"1466bd40-3acf-591c-b003-9c0f787e6551\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4\" :db/id 17592186300044}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"1466bd40-3acf-591c-b003-9c0f787e6551\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4\" :db/id 17592186300044} :answer-field/id #uuid \"aeaa33c7-8e94-592c-baee-0f58e084a228\" :answer-field/key \"field-1\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186301794}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"657285cd-f814-5fb4-ae66-64de44c5741c\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-326246\" :question/problem \"Consider the curve with parametric equations\\n\\n$$\\nx={t}^{3}-2t,\\\\,y=-2t+\\\\frac{3}{2},\\\\,0\\\\le t\\\\le 5.\\n$$\\n\\nFill in the blanks in the following table of values:\\n\\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $0$ | $-1$ | {{field-1}} | $21$ | $56$ | {{field-2}} |\\n| $y$ | $\\\\frac{3}{2}$ | $-\\\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-\\\\frac{5}{2}$ | {{field-3}} | $-\\\\frac{13}{2}$ | $-\\\\frac{17}{2}$ |\" :question/worked-solution \"- To find the value of $x(2),$ we substitute $t=2$ into $x={t}^{3}-2t.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nx(2)=(2)^{3}-2(2)=8-4=4.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $y(3),$ we substitute $t=3$ into $y=-2t+\\\\frac{3}{2}.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\ny(3)=-2(3)+\\\\frac{3}{2}=-6+\\\\frac{3}{2}=-\\\\frac{12}{2}+\\\\frac{3}{2}=-\\\\frac{9}{2}.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $x(5),$ we substitute $t=5$ into $x={t}^{3}-2t.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nx(5)=(5)^{3}-2(5)=125-10=115.\\n$$\\n\\nThen the table is \\n\\n \\n\\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $0$ | $-1$ | $4$ | $21$ | $56$ | $115$ |\\n| $y$ | $\\\\frac{3}{2}$ | $-\\\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-\\\\frac{5}{2}$ | $-\\\\frac{9}{2}$ | $-\\\\frac{13}{2}$ | $-\\\\frac{17}{2}$ |\"} {:db/id 17592186302271 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"d7d2c9b6-3f61-5b0c-8d40-7c8c3ad00a08\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"16\" :db/id 17592186301036}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"d7d2c9b6-3f61-5b0c-8d40-7c8c3ad00a08\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"16\" :db/id 17592186301036} :answer-field/id #uuid \"475eb211-fdac-5ef1-a7b1-d7c876368b09\" :answer-field/key \"field-2\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186301462} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"01f65e8b-4617-531e-b590-48e7cae4c340\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"92\" :db/id 17592186299937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"01f65e8b-4617-531e-b590-48e7cae4c340\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"92\" :db/id 17592186299937} :answer-field/id #uuid \"56a825ae-6d12-5ca9-bc21-522636b5fc85\" :answer-field/key \"field-3\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186301508} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"d7bc2368-2d49-58ef-9f8a-804b443a1d10\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"1\" :db/id 17592186301035}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"d7bc2368-2d49-58ef-9f8a-804b443a1d10\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"1\" :db/id 17592186301035} :answer-field/id #uuid \"ceb7fcf1-d976-5665-b741-fc69d5d0b030\" :answer-field/key \"field-1\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186301890}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"854eb5bf-774c-5c7b-a116-76c300b05cad\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-326247\" :question/problem \"Consider the curve with parametric equations\\n\\n$$\\nx={t}^{2}-2t+2,\\\\,y=2{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}+12,\\\\,-1\\\\le t\\\\le 4.\\n$$\\n\\nFill in the blanks in the following table of values:\\n\\n| **$t$** | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $5$ | $2$ | {{field-1}} | $2$ | $5$ | $10$ |\\n| $y$ | $7$ | $12$ | $11$ | {{field-2}} | $39$ | {{field-3}} |\" :question/worked-solution \"- To find the value of $x(1),$ we substitute $t=1$ into $x={t}^{2}-2t+2.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nx(1)=(1)^{2}-2(1)+2=1-2+2=1.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $y(2),$ we substitute $t=2$ into $y=2{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}+12.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\ny(2)=2(2)^{3}-3(2)^{2}+12=16-12+12=16.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $y(4),$ we substitute $t=4$ into $y=2{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}+12.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\ny(4)=2(4)^{3}-3(4)^{2}+12=128-48+12=92.\\n$$\\n\\nThen the table is \\n\\n \\n\\n| **$t$** | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $5$ | $2$ | $1$ | $2$ | $5$ | $10$ |\\n| $y$ | $7$ | $12$ | $11$ | $16$ | $39$ | $92$ |\"} {:db/id 17592186302272 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"0b2f74f3-79cd-574f-9238-6fcdf77522bb\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{3}\" :db/id 17592186299987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"0b2f74f3-79cd-574f-9238-6fcdf77522bb\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{3}\" :db/id 17592186299987} :answer-field/id #uuid \"27b250f4-4f05-544b-8ebc-03ff71447626\" :answer-field/key \"field-2\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186301351} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"bf5af01e-616b-5c46-a431-35738aad2c1d\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{2}{3}\" :db/id 17592186300920}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"bf5af01e-616b-5c46-a431-35738aad2c1d\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{2}{3}\" :db/id 17592186300920} :answer-field/id #uuid \"cf8b63ee-6e28-54cd-8eb2-72e238c6f9eb\" :answer-field/key \"field-3\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186301894} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"521f8156-1852-5b70-b978-7d31f5f9d99c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{121}{2}\" :db/id 17592186300388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"521f8156-1852-5b70-b978-7d31f5f9d99c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{121}{2}\" :db/id 17592186300388} :answer-field/id #uuid \"ec5a0f5f-9550-5151-a6a5-e2b91e74b30c\" :answer-field/key \"field-1\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186301978}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"b8c7b5c0-57d6-5e10-9424-b187294f0724\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-326250\" :question/problem \"Consider the curve with parametric equations\\n\\n$$\\nx=\\\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{3}-2,\\\\,y=\\\\frac{t-1}{t+1},\\\\,0\\\\le t\\\\le 5.\\n$$\\n\\nFill in the blanks in the following table of values:\\n\\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-\\\\frac{3}{2}$ | $2$ | $\\\\frac{23}{2}$ | $30$ | {{field-1}} |\\n| $y$ | $-1$ | $0$ | {{field-2}} | $\\\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\\\frac{3}{5}$ | {{field-3}} |\" :question/worked-solution \"- To find the value of $x(5),$ we substitute $t=5$ into $x=\\\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{3}-2.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nx(5)=\\\\frac{1}{2}(5)^{3}-2=\\\\frac{125}{2}-\\\\frac{4}{2}=\\\\frac{121}{2}.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $y(2),$ we substitute $t=2$ into $y=\\\\frac{t-1}{t+1}.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\ny(2)=\\\\frac{2-1}{2+1}=\\\\frac{1}{3}.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $y(5),$ we substitute $t=5$ into $y=\\\\frac{t-1}{t+1}.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\ny(0)=\\\\frac{5-1}{5+1}=\\\\frac{4}{6}=\\\\frac{2}{3}.\\n$$\\n\\nThen the table is \\n\\n \\n\\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-\\\\frac{3}{2}$ | $2$ | $\\\\frac{23}{2}$ | $30$ | $\\\\frac{121}{2}$ |\\n| $y$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $\\\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\\\frac{3}{5}$ | $\\\\frac{2}{3}$ |\"} {:db/id 17592186302273 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"dea4c418-a2a3-5eb1-914f-abfb1e44f530\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{5}{2}\" :db/id 17592186301065}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"dea4c418-a2a3-5eb1-914f-abfb1e44f530\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{5}{2}\" :db/id 17592186301065} :answer-field/id #uuid \"0f6a1cf6-f1e9-5324-a0cd-8de8748825b8\" :answer-field/key \"field-2\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186301277} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"42ca4294-13f5-564a-9c61-bfe51e2f5894\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4\" :db/id 17592186300288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"42ca4294-13f5-564a-9c61-bfe51e2f5894\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4\" :db/id 17592186300288} :answer-field/id #uuid \"af402e53-ece3-5170-871d-14635b65690e\" :answer-field/key \"field-3\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186301800} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"3dbec592-362f-5cb8-838b-38b868c54f30\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"1\" :db/id 17592186300263}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"3dbec592-362f-5cb8-838b-38b868c54f30\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"1\" :db/id 17592186300263} :answer-field/id #uuid \"d785ba22-7770-5336-8681-5b6890e427ef\" :answer-field/key \"field-1\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186301920}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"9505d474-040a-5e78-97f1-c782cc218ed5\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-326251\" :question/problem \"Consider the curve with parametric equations\\n\\n$$\\nx=\\\\sqrt{\\\\,t+4\\\\,},\\\\,y=\\\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}-t,\\\\,-3\\\\le t\\\\le 2.\\n$$\\n\\nFill in the blanks in the following table of values:\\n\\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | {{field-1}} | $\\\\sqrt{2}$ | $\\\\sqrt{3}$ | $2$ | $\\\\sqrt{5}$ | $\\\\sqrt{6}$ |\\n| $y$ | $\\\\frac{33}{2}$ | $8$ | {{field-2}} | $0$ | $\\\\frac{1}{2}$ | {{field-3}} |\" :question/worked-solution \"- To find the value of $x(-3),$ we substitute $t=-3$ into $x=\\\\sqrt{\\\\,t+4\\\\,}.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nx(-3)=\\\\sqrt{-3+4}=\\\\sqrt{1}=1.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $y(-1),$ we substitute $t=-1$ into $y=\\\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}-t.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\ny(-1)=\\\\frac{3}{2}(-1)^{2}-(-1)=\\\\frac{3}{2}+1=\\\\frac{3}{2}+\\\\frac{2}{2}=\\\\frac{5}{2}.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $y(2),$ we substitute $t=2$ into $y=\\\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}-t.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\ny(2)=\\\\frac{3}{2}(2)^{2}-(2)=6-2=4.\\n$$\\n\\nThen the table is \\n\\n \\n\\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $1$ | $\\\\sqrt{2}$ | $\\\\sqrt{3}$ | $2$ | $\\\\sqrt{5}$ | $\\\\sqrt{6}$ |\\n| $y$ | $\\\\frac{33}{2}$ | $8$ | $\\\\frac{5}{2}$ | $0$ | $\\\\frac{1}{2}$ | $4$ |\"} {:db/id 17592186302274 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"503204c2-5202-5eb6-9c99-1d89a4256bc4\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"1\" :db/id 17592186300382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"503204c2-5202-5eb6-9c99-1d89a4256bc4\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"1\" :db/id 17592186300382} :answer-field/id #uuid \"775ffea0-6f09-507b-ba4a-f5929a9c5ece\" :answer-field/key \"field-2\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186301596} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"20d2ae08-199c-5474-adf2-cfd379ea5346\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{2}\" :db/id 17592186300115}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"20d2ae08-199c-5474-adf2-cfd379ea5346\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{2}\" :db/id 17592186300115} :answer-field/id #uuid \"9fdb03f8-a8af-5dff-897a-1a48b028739f\" :answer-field/key \"field-3\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186301740} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"8236cfbf-50c1-52a1-9051-6e2573a692b6\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"0\" :db/id 17592186300611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"8236cfbf-50c1-52a1-9051-6e2573a692b6\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"0\" :db/id 17592186300611} :answer-field/id #uuid \"be04d349-7486-598b-9dcd-fc83d123cadf\" :answer-field/key \"field-1\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186301846}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"cefa32c2-7378-5ecb-a3a0-9b87e829889e\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-326255\" :question/problem \"Consider the curve with parametric equations\\n\\n$$\\nx=cos\\\\,\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi t}{4}\\\\right),\\\\,y=sin\\\\,\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi t}{6}\\\\right),\\\\,0\\\\le t\\\\le 5.\\n$$\\n\\nFill in the blanks in the following table of values:\\n\\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $1$ | $\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ | {{field-1}} | $-\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ | $-1$ | $-\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ |\\n| $y$ | $0$ | $\\\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} | $\\\\frac{1}{2}$ |\" :question/worked-solution \"- To find the value of $x(2),$ we substitute $t=2$ into $x=cos\\\\,\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi t}{4}\\\\right).$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nx(2)=cos\\\\,\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi (2)}{4}\\\\right)=cos\\\\,\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{2}\\\\right)=0.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $y(3),$ we substitute $t=3$ into $y=sin\\\\,\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi t}{6}\\\\right).$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\ny(3)=sin\\\\,\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi (3)}{6}\\\\right)=sin\\\\,\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{2}\\\\right)=1.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $y(4),$ we substitute $t=4$ into $y=sin\\\\,\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi t}{6}\\\\right).$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\ny(1)=sin\\\\,\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi (4)}{6}\\\\right)=sin\\\\,\\\\left(\\\\frac{2\\\\pi }{3}\\\\right)=\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\n$$\\n\\nThen the table is \\n\\n \\n\\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $1$ | $\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ | $0$ | $-\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ | $-1$ | $-\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ |\\n| $y$ | $0$ | $\\\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $1$ | $\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $\\\\frac{1}{2}$ |\"} {:db/id 17592186302275 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"0cda53e7-8da8-5d86-a98c-5728719bc41b\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\sqrt{3}\" :db/id 17592186300000}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"0cda53e7-8da8-5d86-a98c-5728719bc41b\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\sqrt{3}\" :db/id 17592186300000} :answer-field/id #uuid \"926f273e-d8b0-5e4d-9631-40e611c24ed3\" :answer-field/key \"field-3\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186301693} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"25f796a4-f9bc-52c2-95c4-861c28462e0f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-1\" :db/id 17592186300143}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"25f796a4-f9bc-52c2-95c4-861c28462e0f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-1\" :db/id 17592186300143} :answer-field/id #uuid \"d4c15bfd-ddd4-56df-9248-59fef4cfb8ff\" :answer-field/key \"field-2\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186301912} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"011fae4e-c40e-5543-bf07-c0c1656584a7\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"1\" :db/id 17592186299934}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"011fae4e-c40e-5543-bf07-c0c1656584a7\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"1\" :db/id 17592186299934} :answer-field/id #uuid \"da7a0f49-5d74-598d-9cc7-a44f9d26dfa4\" :answer-field/key \"field-1\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186301928}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"e9040c3c-4511-5ef7-a719-36ef3ae85af2\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-326256\" :question/problem \"Consider the curve with parametric equations\\n\\n$$\\nx=cos\\\\,\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi t}{2}\\\\right),\\\\,y=tan\\\\,\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi t}{3}\\\\right),\\\\,-1\\\\le t\\\\le 4.\\n$$\\n\\nFill in the blanks in the following table of values:\\n\\n| **$t$** | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} | $0$ | {{field-2}} | $0$ | $1$ |\\n| $y$ | $-\\\\sqrt{3}$ | $0$ | {{field-3}} | $-\\\\sqrt{3}$ | $0$ | $\\\\sqrt{3}$ |\" :question/worked-solution \"- To find the value of $x(0),$ we substitute $t=0$ into $x=cos\\\\,\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi t}{2}\\\\right).$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nx(0)=cos\\\\,\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi (0)}{2}\\\\right)=\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=1.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $y(1),$ we substitute $t=1$ into $y=tan\\\\,\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi t}{3}\\\\right).$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\ny(1)=tan\\\\,\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi (1)}{3}\\\\right)=tan\\\\,\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{3}\\\\right)=\\\\sqrt{3}.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $x(2),$ we substitute $t=2$ into $x=cos\\\\,\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi t}{2}\\\\right).$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nx(2)=cos\\\\,\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi (2)}{2}\\\\right)=\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\\\pi )=-1.\\n$$\\n\\nThen the table is \\n\\n \\n\\n| **$t$** | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\\n| $y$ | $-\\\\sqrt{3}$ | $0$ | $\\\\sqrt{3}$ | $-\\\\sqrt{3}$ | $0$ | $\\\\sqrt{3}$ |\"} {:db/id 17592186335928 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"054e45cb-ef1a-592f-8ce5-2215be471cc4\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"7\" :db/id 17592186333032} {:answer/id #uuid \"79eda04b-781c-5fda-aa4a-bb2479352bdd\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3\" :db/id 17592186334085} {:answer/id #uuid \"9a6d0cbe-1f59-57f6-aefd-5d53e15a7b1d\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-6\" :db/id 17592186334353} {:answer/id #uuid \"b7b9a71e-ffbd-5091-8899-773c38323464\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"5\" :db/id 17592186334599} {:answer/id #uuid \"ecb2865c-3deb-55d1-a152-eed996480e2f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-4\" :db/id 17592186335064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"b7b9a71e-ffbd-5091-8899-773c38323464\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"5\" :db/id 17592186334599} :answer-field/id #uuid \"fcd68d1f-2e2e-53b3-8c88-e40a6b095d8e\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186335680}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"e9a5f727-046e-5c6d-b3a8-b57aa0e0de57\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-6742\" :question/problem \"For the parametric curve\\n\\n$$\\nx=t+1,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,y={t}^{2}-6,-3\\\\le t\\\\le 3,\\n$$\\n\\nconsider the following table of values:\\n\\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | ${\\\\color{blue}c}$ |\\n| $y$ | ${\\\\color{blue}a}$ | $-2$ | $-5$ | ${\\\\color{blue}b}$ | $-5$ | $-2$ | $3$ |\\n\\n\\n\\nFind the value of $a-b-c.$\" :question/worked-solution \"- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=-3$ into $y={t}^{2}-6.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\na=(-3)^{2}-6=9-6=3.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=0$ into $y={t}^{2}-6.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nb={0}^{2}-6=0-6=-6.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=3$ into $x=t+1.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nc=3+1=4.\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, we have\\n\\n$$\\na-b-c=3-(-6)-4=5.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186335959 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"06ea7064-8984-5ac6-91ea-ed8921bbc138\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3\" :db/id 17592186333056} {:answer/id #uuid \"827b89fe-a572-54cd-b9cb-dcc0569b217e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-2\" :db/id 17592186334153} {:answer/id #uuid \"c8f91035-840a-59fe-a14a-8ded740896f0\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"1\" :db/id 17592186334736} {:answer/id #uuid \"d3a7c0bf-869c-5788-8888-00b2ca3dcdac\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"0\" :db/id 17592186334846} {:answer/id #uuid \"ed2e747f-c905-58fc-9adb-fb9c26ba7608\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-1\" :db/id 17592186335069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"827b89fe-a572-54cd-b9cb-dcc0569b217e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-2\" :db/id 17592186334153} :answer-field/id #uuid \"4a546347-737e-5d85-bf73-af24c4b5c1f5\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186335386}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"f35c183e-5200-5f54-ad21-69984c940bed\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-6825\" :question/problem \"For the parametric curve\\n\\n$$\\nx=3t-2,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,y=\\\\frac{10}{{t}^{2}+1},\\\\,-3\\\\le t\\\\le 3,\\n$$\\n\\nconsider the following table of values:\\n\\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | ${\\\\color{blue}a}$ | $-8$ | $-5$ | $-2$ | $1$ | $4$ | ${\\\\color{blue}c}$ |\\n| $y$ | $1$ | ${\\\\color{blue}b}$ | $5$ | $10$ | $5$ | $2$ | $1$ |\\n\\n\\n\\nFind the value of $a+b+c.$\" :question/worked-solution \"- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=-3$ into $x=3t-2.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\na=3(-3)-2=-9-2=-11.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=-2$ into $y=\\\\frac{10}{{t}^{2}+1}.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nb=\\\\frac{10}{(-2)^{2}+1}=\\\\frac{10}{5}=2.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=3$ into $x=3t-2.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nc=3(3)-2=9-2=7.\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, we have\\n\\n$$\\na+b+c=-11+2+7=-2.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186336019 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"06475ed3-8f81-5f2a-92d7-37b61ba3d841\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-13\" :db/id 17592186333047} {:answer/id #uuid \"1675a734-ba42-53ad-bacc-d3d9a7ecfb02\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-10\" :db/id 17592186333190} {:answer/id #uuid \"379b5cc9-a398-5f20-b13a-5820843260de\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"15\" :db/id 17592186333501} {:answer/id #uuid \"4e027385-3e35-564e-88cf-8f5955ad0320\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"12\" :db/id 17592186333708} {:answer/id #uuid \"bbabf68e-a37c-54df-b8af-32120f8b5dfd\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"8\" :db/id 17592186334625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"06475ed3-8f81-5f2a-92d7-37b61ba3d841\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-13\" :db/id 17592186333047} :answer-field/id #uuid \"be306b92-cfe4-5ecc-9451-b14d1a1a3e42\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186335589}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"cc1d2bf2-3dfe-5506-8434-072c2dc13cdb\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-69922\" :question/problem \"For the parametric curve\\n\\n$$\\nx=2t+1,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,y=2t-1,\\\\,0\\\\le t\\\\le 5,\\n$$\\n\\nconsider the following table of values:\\n\\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $1$ | $3$ | ${\\\\color{blue}b}$ | $7$ | $9$ | $11$ |\\n| $y$ | ${\\\\color{blue}a}$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ | ${\\\\color{blue}c}$ | $9$ |\\n\\n\\n\\nFind the value of $a-b-c.$\" :question/worked-solution \"- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=0$ into $y=2t-1.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\na=2(0)-1=0-1=-1.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=2$ into $x=2t+1.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nb=2(2)+1=4+1=5.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=4$ into $y=2t-1.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nc=2(4)-1=8-1=7.\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, we have\\n\\n$$\\na-b-c=-1-5-7=-13.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186557627 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"fb9a309f-94bc-51a2-869f-3b3a9041caa5\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{7}{4}\" :db/id 17592186557695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"fb9a309f-94bc-51a2-869f-3b3a9041caa5\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{7}{4}\" :db/id 17592186557695} :answer-field/id #uuid \"2358b114-00ed-5898-b286-205889192af5\" :answer-field/key \"field-2\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186557636} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"3fe8cfd3-e0cc-5393-a292-993c1116bc49\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{41}{3}\" :db/id 17592186557641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"3fe8cfd3-e0cc-5393-a292-993c1116bc49\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{41}{3}\" :db/id 17592186557641} :answer-field/id #uuid \"677c5a85-d33c-5340-9e9f-244d2e3567b2\" :answer-field/key \"field-1\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186557658} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"ab59f56d-b3cc-5819-b89e-a111f64fab73\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{94}{3}\" :db/id 17592186557675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"ab59f56d-b3cc-5819-b89e-a111f64fab73\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{94}{3}\" :db/id 17592186557675} :answer-field/id #uuid \"94933d06-9871-5cc2-9edb-a456dd9744da\" :answer-field/key \"field-3\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186557667}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"0ab26a74-291b-5410-83ed-7e43a17199d1\" :question/problem \"Consider the curve with parametric equations\\n\\n$$\\nx=- \\\\frac{5 t^{2}}{4} - \\\\frac{4 t}{3} - 6,\\\\,y=- \\\\frac{3 t^{2}}{4} - \\\\frac{t}{3} + 6,\\\\,0\\\\le t\\\\le 5.\\n$$\\n\\nFill in the blanks in the following table of values:\\n\\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $-6$ | $- \\\\frac{103}{12}$ | {{field-1}} | $- \\\\frac{85}{4}$ | {{field-3}} | $- \\\\frac{527}{12}$ |\\n| $y$ | $6$ | $\\\\frac{59}{12}$ | $\\\\frac{7}{3}$ | {{field-2}} | $- \\\\frac{22}{3}$ | $- \\\\frac{173}{12}$ |\" :question/worked-solution \"- To find the value of $x(2),$ we substitute $t=2$ into $$\\n\\\\displaystyle x=- \\\\frac{5 t^{2}}{4} - \\\\frac{4 t}{3} - 6.\\n$$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nx(2)=- \\\\frac{5 (2)^{2}}{4} - \\\\frac{4 (2)}{3} - 6=(-6)+(-5)+\\\\left(- \\\\frac{8}{3}\\\\right)=- \\\\frac{41}{3}.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $y(3),$ we substitute $t=3$ into $$\\n\\\\displaystyle y=- \\\\frac{3 t^{2}}{4} - \\\\frac{t}{3} + 6.\\n$$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\ny(3)=- \\\\frac{3 (3)^{2}}{4} - \\\\frac{(3)}{3} + 6=(6)+\\\\left(- \\\\frac{27}{4}\\\\right)+(-1)=- \\\\frac{7}{4}.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $x(4),$ we substitute $t=4$ into $$\\n\\\\displaystyle x=- \\\\frac{5 t^{2}}{4} - \\\\frac{4 t}{3} - 6.\\n$$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nx(4)=- \\\\frac{5 (4)^{2}}{4} - \\\\frac{4 (4)}{3} - 6=(-6)+(-20)+\\\\left(- \\\\frac{16}{3}\\\\right)=- \\\\frac{94}{3}.\\n$$\\n\\nThen the table is\\n\\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $-6$ | $- \\\\frac{103}{12}$ | $- \\\\frac{41}{3}$ | $- \\\\frac{85}{4}$ | $- \\\\frac{94}{3}$ | $- \\\\frac{527}{12}$ |\\n| $y$ | $6$ | $\\\\frac{59}{12}$ | $\\\\frac{7}{3}$ | $- \\\\frac{7}{4}$ | $- \\\\frac{22}{3}$ | $- \\\\frac{173}{12}$ |\"} {:db/id 17592186557631 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"9bd1951c-0602-55a5-8645-0789fe856a88\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{25}{3}\" :db/id 17592186557671}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"9bd1951c-0602-55a5-8645-0789fe856a88\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{25}{3}\" :db/id 17592186557671} :answer-field/id #uuid \"55ebcdaa-54ae-5f9c-bb83-2fab47dcd1f6\" :answer-field/key \"field-1\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186557651} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"591b377a-f05f-55a2-80e5-1390a0863f4f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{56}{3}\" :db/id 17592186557654}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"591b377a-f05f-55a2-80e5-1390a0863f4f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{56}{3}\" :db/id 17592186557654} :answer-field/id #uuid \"656eda5e-1958-5e69-9543-aece5e8c6dcf\" :answer-field/key \"field-3\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186557656} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"08441e59-4936-522c-94dc-e808225422f2\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{9}{4}\" :db/id 17592186557626}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"08441e59-4936-522c-94dc-e808225422f2\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{9}{4}\" :db/id 17592186557626} :answer-field/id #uuid \"66fd5de2-d0f1-5abd-9945-24b9ffb7f3b3\" :answer-field/key \"field-2\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186557657}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"196444c1-2873-57fb-a693-e030a15fb6c7\" :question/problem \"Consider the curve with parametric equations\\n\\n$$\\nx=\\\\frac{3 t^{2}}{4} + \\\\frac{2 t}{3} + 4,\\\\,y=\\\\frac{t^{2}}{4} + \\\\frac{4 t}{3} - 4,\\\\,0\\\\le t\\\\le 5.\\n$$\\n\\nFill in the blanks in the following table of values:\\n\\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $4$ | $\\\\frac{65}{12}$ | {{field-1}} | $\\\\frac{51}{4}$ | {{field-3}} | $\\\\frac{313}{12}$ |\\n| $y$ | $-4$ | $- \\\\frac{29}{12}$ | $- \\\\frac{1}{3}$ | {{field-2}} | $\\\\frac{16}{3}$ | $\\\\frac{107}{12}$ |\" :question/worked-solution \"- To find the value of $x(2),$ we substitute $t=2$ into $$\\n\\\\displaystyle x=\\\\frac{3 t^{2}}{4} + \\\\frac{2 t}{3} + 4.\\n$$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nx(2)=\\\\frac{3 (2)^{2}}{4} + \\\\frac{2 (2)}{3} + 4=(4)+\\\\left(\\\\frac{4}{3}\\\\right)+(3)=\\\\frac{25}{3}.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $y(3),$ we substitute $t=3$ into $y=\\\\frac{t^{2}}{4} + \\\\frac{4 t}{3} - 4.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\ny(3)=\\\\frac{(3)^{2}}{4} + \\\\frac{4 (3)}{3} - 4=(-4)+\\\\left(\\\\frac{9}{4}\\\\right)+(4)=\\\\frac{9}{4}.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $x(4),$ we substitute $t=4$ into $$\\n\\\\displaystyle x=\\\\frac{3 t^{2}}{4} + \\\\frac{2 t}{3} + 4.\\n$$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nx(4)=\\\\frac{3 (4)^{2}}{4} + \\\\frac{2 (4)}{3} + 4=(4)+\\\\left(\\\\frac{8}{3}\\\\right)+(12)=\\\\frac{56}{3}.\\n$$\\n\\nThen the table is\\n\\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $4$ | $\\\\frac{65}{12}$ | $\\\\frac{25}{3}$ | $\\\\frac{51}{4}$ | $\\\\frac{56}{3}$ | $\\\\frac{313}{12}$ |\\n| $y$ | $-4$ | $- \\\\frac{29}{12}$ | $- \\\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\\\frac{9}{4}$ | $\\\\frac{16}{3}$ | $\\\\frac{107}{12}$ |\"} {:db/id 17592186557649 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"4315c1ff-ffd7-588d-8cad-759c7a46b437\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{46}{3}\" :db/id 17592186557644}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"4315c1ff-ffd7-588d-8cad-759c7a46b437\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{46}{3}\" :db/id 17592186557644} :answer-field/id #uuid \"4c6f52c7-bcfe-58f1-aa24-71f8de81c715\" :answer-field/key \"field-3\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186557647} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"1e89b512-8b8e-5a63-ac8e-644d86b1db26\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{15}{4}\" :db/id 17592186557634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"1e89b512-8b8e-5a63-ac8e-644d86b1db26\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{15}{4}\" :db/id 17592186557634} :answer-field/id #uuid \"861c1249-4ee1-5faa-9e25-a294aec0cf13\" :answer-field/key \"field-2\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186557665} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"c2ad1837-3eae-5b4d-8b93-ece727038234\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{8}{3}\" :db/id 17592186557686}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"c2ad1837-3eae-5b4d-8b93-ece727038234\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{8}{3}\" :db/id 17592186557686} :answer-field/id #uuid \"99423b3a-c681-5aa6-891c-9cf8a79ccb76\" :answer-field/key \"field-1\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186557669}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"51b8d9af-e12b-59bd-a1bf-d1f0e6dac58b\" :question/problem \"Consider the curve with parametric equations\\n\\n$$\\nx=\\\\frac{t^{3}}{4} + \\\\frac{t^{2}}{3} - 6,\\\\,y=- \\\\frac{t^{3}}{4} + \\\\frac{2 t^{2}}{3} - 3,\\\\,0\\\\le t\\\\le 5.\\n$$\\n\\nFill in the blanks in the following table of values:\\n\\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $-6$ | $- \\\\frac{65}{12}$ | {{field-1}} | $\\\\frac{15}{4}$ | {{field-3}} | $\\\\frac{403}{12}$ |\\n| $y$ | $-3$ | $- \\\\frac{31}{12}$ | $- \\\\frac{7}{3}$ | {{field-2}} | $- \\\\frac{25}{3}$ | $- \\\\frac{211}{12}$ |\" :question/worked-solution \"- To find the value of $x(2),$ we substitute $t=2$ into $$\\n\\\\displaystyle x=\\\\frac{t^{3}}{4} + \\\\frac{t^{2}}{3} - 6.\\n$$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nx(2)=\\\\frac{(2)^{3}}{4} + \\\\frac{(2)^{2}}{3} - 6=(-6)+\\\\left(\\\\frac{4}{3}\\\\right)+(2)=- \\\\frac{8}{3}.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $y(3),$ we substitute $t=3$ into $$\\n\\\\displaystyle y=- \\\\frac{t^{3}}{4} + \\\\frac{2 t^{2}}{3} - 3.\\n$$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\ny(3)=- \\\\frac{(3)^{3}}{4} + \\\\frac{2 (3)^{2}}{3} - 3=(-3)+\\\\left(- \\\\frac{27}{4}\\\\right)+(6)=- \\\\frac{15}{4}.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $x(4),$ we substitute $t=4$ into $$\\n\\\\displaystyle x=\\\\frac{t^{3}}{4} + \\\\frac{t^{2}}{3} - 6.\\n$$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nx(4)=\\\\frac{(4)^{3}}{4} + \\\\frac{(4)^{2}}{3} - 6=(-6)+\\\\left(\\\\frac{16}{3}\\\\right)+(16)=\\\\frac{46}{3}.\\n$$\\n\\nThen the table is\\n\\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $-6$ | $- \\\\frac{65}{12}$ | $- \\\\frac{8}{3}$ | $\\\\frac{15}{4}$ | $\\\\frac{46}{3}$ | $\\\\frac{403}{12}$ |\\n| $y$ | $-3$ | $- \\\\frac{31}{12}$ | $- \\\\frac{7}{3}$ | $- \\\\frac{15}{4}$ | $- \\\\frac{25}{3}$ | $- \\\\frac{211}{12}$ |\"} {:db/id 17592186557664 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"1aa1dd71-26b4-591d-b8f8-f06dcd091ab7\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{13}{4}\" :db/id 17592186557632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"1aa1dd71-26b4-591d-b8f8-f06dcd091ab7\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{13}{4}\" :db/id 17592186557632} :answer-field/id #uuid \"366da810-500e-5a59-a5e9-ceb2aeaa8bf2\" :answer-field/key \"field-2\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186557639} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"a71bf98b-8bc6-575e-a23e-53a557bcd7ea\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{2}{3}\" :db/id 17592186557673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"a71bf98b-8bc6-575e-a23e-53a557bcd7ea\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{2}{3}\" :db/id 17592186557673} :answer-field/id #uuid \"bd9a794b-271c-5853-9561-69ad961a36cb\" :answer-field/key \"field-3\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186557681} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"227b7980-e43b-5438-a13d-5a67588ba3d6\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{13}{3}\" :db/id 17592186557635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"227b7980-e43b-5438-a13d-5a67588ba3d6\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{13}{3}\" :db/id 17592186557635} :answer-field/id #uuid \"c4c181a7-04cd-5aea-9742-ab16b8c53197\" :answer-field/key \"field-1\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186557687}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"8115ffdf-d0da-5624-ae18-eff4552c71e2\" :question/problem \"Consider the curve with parametric equations\\n\\n$$\\nx=\\\\frac{t^{2}}{4} + \\\\frac{t}{3} - 6,\\\\,y=- \\\\frac{t^{2}}{4} + \\\\frac{2 t}{3} - 3,\\\\,0\\\\le t\\\\le 5.\\n$$\\n\\nFill in the blanks in the following table of values:\\n\\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $-6$ | $- \\\\frac{65}{12}$ | {{field-1}} | $- \\\\frac{11}{4}$ | {{field-3}} | $\\\\frac{23}{12}$ |\\n| $y$ | $-3$ | $- \\\\frac{31}{12}$ | $- \\\\frac{8}{3}$ | {{field-2}} | $- \\\\frac{13}{3}$ | $- \\\\frac{71}{12}$ |\" :question/worked-solution \"- To find the value of $x(2),$ we substitute $t=2$ into $x=\\\\frac{t^{2}}{4} + \\\\frac{t}{3} - 6.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nx(2)=\\\\frac{(2)^{2}}{4} + \\\\frac{(2)}{3} - 6=(-6)+\\\\left(\\\\frac{2}{3}\\\\right)+(1)=- \\\\frac{13}{3}.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $y(3),$ we substitute $t=3$ into $$\\n\\\\displaystyle y=- \\\\frac{t^{2}}{4} + \\\\frac{2 t}{3} - 3.\\n$$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\ny(3)=- \\\\frac{(3)^{2}}{4} + \\\\frac{2 (3)}{3} - 3=(-3)+\\\\left(- \\\\frac{9}{4}\\\\right)+(2)=- \\\\frac{13}{4}.\\n$$\\n\\n- To find the value of $x(4),$ we substitute $t=4$ into $x=\\\\frac{t^{2}}{4} + \\\\frac{t}{3} - 6.$ This gives\\n\\n$$\\nx(4)=\\\\frac{(4)^{2}}{4} + \\\\frac{(4)}{3} - 6=(-6)+\\\\left(\\\\frac{4}{3}\\\\right)+(4)=- \\\\frac{2}{3}.\\n$$\\n\\nThen the table is\\n\\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| $x$ | $-6$ | $- \\\\frac{65}{12}$ | $- \\\\frac{13}{3}$ | $- \\\\frac{11}{4}$ | $- \\\\frac{2}{3}$ | $\\\\frac{23}{12}$ |\\n| $y$ | $-3$ | $- \\\\frac{31}{12}$ | $- \\\\frac{8}{3}$ | $- \\\\frac{13}{4}$ | $- \\\\frac{13}{3}$ | $- \\\\frac{71}{12}$ |\"} {:db/id 17592186557666 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"d4cf8d31-d1ba-5e3e-b23f-5f14f0b6f0d0\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\f