      "question": {
        ":question/id": "90febdeb-888f-5245-a4c0-d005214c232c",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=2 - t^{2},\\qquad y=- 3 t - 3,\\qquad -2\\le t\\le 2.\n$$\n\nFill in the three blanks in the table. Give exact values.\n\nUse the value of $t$ at the top of each column in the formula for that row. For example, $x(-2)=2 - \\left(-2\\right)^{2}=-2$.\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $1$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $y$ | $3$ | $0$ | $-3$ |\n\n| **$t$** | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $y$ | {{field-2}} | $-9$ |",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The missing entry is in the $x$-row under $t=0$. Substitute into $x=2 - t^{2}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) &=2 - \\left(0\\right)^{2} \\\\ &=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $y$-row under $t=1$. Substitute into $y=- 3 t - 3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) &=- 3 \\left(1\\right) - 3 \\\\ &=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $x$-row under $t=2$. Substitute into $x=2 - t^{2}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(2) &=2 - \\left(2\\right)^{2} \\\\ &=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe completed table is\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| $y$ | $3$ | $0$ | $-3$ |\n\n| **$t$** | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $-2$ |\n| $y$ | $-6$ | $-9$ |",
