    {
      "knowledge_point": {
        "db_id": 17592186087717,
        "id": "bbf50e27-a8c3-52e7-be21-5d7ed61e5512",
        "title": "Filling a Table of Values for a Parametric Curve"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "27567bdc-9f35-5be9-8b03-2accae833e9c",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=- t^{2} - 1,\\qquad y=- t - 1,\\qquad -2\\le t\\le 2.\n$$\n\nFill in the three blanks in the table. Give exact values.\n\nUse the value of $t$ at the top of each column in the formula for that row. For example, $x(0)=- \\left(0\\right)^{2} - 1=-1$.\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | {{field-3}} | {{field-1}} | $-1$ |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $0$ | $-1$ |\n\n| **$t$** | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-5$ |\n| $y$ | $-2$ | {{field-2}} |",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The missing entry is in the $x$-row under $t=-1$. Substitute into $x=- t^{2} - 1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(-1) &=- \\left(-1\\right)^{2} - 1 \\\\ &=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $y$-row under $t=2$. Substitute into $y=- t - 1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(2) &=- \\left(2\\right) - 1 \\\\ &=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $x$-row under $t=-2$. Substitute into $x=- t^{2} - 1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(-2) &=- \\left(-2\\right)^{2} - 1 \\\\ &=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe completed table is\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-5$ | $-2$ | $-1$ |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $0$ | $-1$ |\n\n| **$t$** | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-5$ |\n| $y$ | $-2$ | $-3$ |",
