    {
      "knowledge_point": {
        "db_id": 17592186087717,
        "id": "bbf50e27-a8c3-52e7-be21-5d7ed61e5512",
        "title": "Filling a Table of Values for a Parametric Curve"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "bc401fc2-0741-5e28-ac23-67f5c0316d34",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/problem": "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{t + 5},\\qquad y=t^{2} + t + 1,\\qquad -2\\le t\\le 2.\n$$\n\nFill in the three blanks in the table. Give exact values.\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $2$ | $\\sqrt{5}$ |\n| $y$ | {{field-2}} | $1$ | {{field-3}} |\n\n| **$t$** | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $\\sqrt{6}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $y$ | $3$ | $7$ |",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The missing entry is in the $x$-row under $t=2$. Substitute into $x=\\sqrt{t + 5}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(2) &=\\sqrt{\\left(2\\right) + 5} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $y$-row under $t=-2$. Substitute into $y=t^{2} + t + 1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(-2) &=\\left(-2\\right)^{2} + \\left(-2\\right) + 1 \\\\ &=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $y$-row under $t=0$. Substitute into $y=t^{2} + t + 1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) &=\\left(0\\right)^{2} + \\left(0\\right) + 1 \\\\ &=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe completed table is\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $2$ | $\\sqrt{5}$ |\n| $y$ | $3$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n\n| **$t$** | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $\\sqrt{6}$ | $\\sqrt{7}$ |\n| $y$ | $3$ | $7$ |",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "9f08cea1-222d-5521-a1b6-f722bf34659a",
