        "id": "bbf50e27-a8c3-52e7-be21-5d7ed61e5512",
        "title": "Filling a Table of Values for a Parametric Curve"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "ae109e7c-040d-5915-83ac-8deca83290cb",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/problem": "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=- t^{3} - 2 t - 2,\\qquad y=t - 1,\\qquad -2\\le t\\le 2.\n$$\n\nFill in the three blanks in the table. Give exact values.\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $10$ | $1$ | $-2$ |\n| $y$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | {{field-3}} |\n\n| **$t$** | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | {{field-1}} | $-14$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | {{field-2}} |",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The missing entry is in the $x$-row under $t=1$. Substitute into $x=- t^{3} - 2 t - 2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(1) &=- \\left(1\\right)^{3} - 2 \\left(1\\right) - 2 \\\\ &=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $y$-row under $t=2$. Substitute into $y=t - 1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(2) &=\\left(2\\right) - 1 \\\\ &=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $y$-row under $t=0$. Substitute into $y=t - 1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) &=\\left(0\\right) - 1 \\\\ &=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe completed table is\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $10$ | $1$ | $-2$ |\n| $y$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ |\n\n| **$t$** | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-5$ | $-14$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ |",
