    {
      "knowledge_point": {
        "db_id": 17592186087717,
        "id": "bbf50e27-a8c3-52e7-be21-5d7ed61e5512",
        "title": "Filling a Table of Values for a Parametric Curve"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "9041a575-6f1d-552b-b837-3cb6733640f8",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/problem": "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=- \\sqrt{t + 3},\\qquad y=t^{2} - t - 1,\\qquad -2\\le t\\le 2.\n$$\n\nFill in the three blanks in the table. Give exact values.\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $- \\sqrt{2}$ | $- \\sqrt{3}$ |\n| $y$ | $5$ | {{field-2}} | $-1$ |\n\n| **$t$** | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | {{field-3}} | {{field-1}} |\n| $y$ | $-1$ | $1$ |",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The missing entry is in the $x$-row under $t=2$. Substitute into $x=- \\sqrt{t + 3}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(2) &=- \\sqrt{\\left(2\\right) + 3} \\\\ &=- \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $y$-row under $t=-1$. Substitute into $y=t^{2} - t - 1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(-1) &=\\left(-1\\right)^{2} - \\left(-1\\right) - 1 \\\\ &=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $x$-row under $t=1$. Substitute into $x=- \\sqrt{t + 3}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(1) &=- \\sqrt{\\left(1\\right) + 3} \\\\ &=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe completed table is\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $- \\sqrt{2}$ | $- \\sqrt{3}$ |\n| $y$ | $5$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n\n| **$t$** | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $- \\sqrt{5}$ |\n| $y$ | $-1$ | $1$ |",
