      "question": {
        ":question/id": "38db0909-2ecc-5349-b5e3-51ee53a611f3",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/problem": "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=- 2 t - 2,\\qquad y=- t^{3} + t - 2,\\qquad -2\\le t\\le 2.\n$$\n\nFill in the three blanks in the table. Give exact values.\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $2$ | {{field-3}} | $-2$ |\n| $y$ | $4$ | $-2$ | {{field-1}} |\n\n| **$t$** | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-6$ |\n| $y$ | $-2$ | {{field-2}} |",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The missing entry is in the $y$-row under $t=0$. Substitute into $y=- t^{3} + t - 2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) &=- \\left(0\\right)^{3} + \\left(0\\right) - 2 \\\\ &=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $y$-row under $t=2$. Substitute into $y=- t^{3} + t - 2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(2) &=- \\left(2\\right)^{3} + \\left(2\\right) - 2 \\\\ &=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $x$-row under $t=-1$. Substitute into $x=- 2 t - 2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(-1) &=- 2 \\left(-1\\right) - 2 \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe completed table is\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $2$ | $0$ | $-2$ |\n| $y$ | $4$ | $-2$ | $-2$ |\n\n| **$t$** | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-6$ |\n| $y$ | $-2$ | $-8$ |",
