    {
      "knowledge_point": {
        "db_id": 17592186087717,
        "id": "bbf50e27-a8c3-52e7-be21-5d7ed61e5512",
        "title": "Filling a Table of Values for a Parametric Curve"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "7ffd2df9-6212-5ff4-bae5-4c049e9f941a",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/problem": "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=t^{2} - t - 2,\\qquad y=\\frac{t + 1}{t + 4},\\qquad -2\\le t\\le 2.\n$$\n\nFill in the three blanks in the table. Give exact values.\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | {{field-3}} | $0$ | $-2$ |\n| $y$ | $- \\frac{1}{2}$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} |\n\n| **$t$** | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | {{field-2}} | $0$ |\n| $y$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The missing entry is in the $y$-row under $t=0$. Substitute into $y=\\frac{t + 1}{t + 4}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) &=\\frac{\\left(0\\right) + 1}{\\left(0\\right) + 4} \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $x$-row under $t=1$. Substitute into $x=t^{2} - t - 2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(1) &=\\left(1\\right)^{2} - \\left(1\\right) - 2 \\\\ &=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $x$-row under $t=-2$. Substitute into $x=t^{2} - t - 2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(-2) &=\\left(-2\\right)^{2} - \\left(-2\\right) - 2 \\\\ &=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe completed table is\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $4$ | $0$ | $-2$ |\n| $y$ | $- \\frac{1}{2}$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n\n| **$t$** | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $0$ |\n| $y$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "7481c2c2-315a-530b-aff1-6d7af617d6d1",
            ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
