        ":question/worked-solution": "The $a$ entry is in the $x$-row under $t=0$. Substitute into $x=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{6}\\right)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a &=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi \\left(0\\right)}{6}\\right) \\\\ &=\\sin\\left(0\\right) \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $b$ entry is in the $y$-row under $t=-1$. Substitute into $y=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{4}\\right)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b &=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi \\left(-1\\right)}{4}\\right) \\\\ &=\\cos\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $c$ entry is in the $y$-row under $t=1$. Substitute into $y=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{4}\\right)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c &=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi \\left(1\\right)}{4}\\right) \\\\ &=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute the three entries with the signs in the requested expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}a+b+c \\\\ =\\left(0\\right)+\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\ =\\sqrt{2}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nThe completed table is\n\n| **$t$** | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $- \\frac{1}{2}$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $y$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ | $1$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ |\n\n| **$t$** | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ |\n| $y$ | $- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ | $-1$ |",
