    {
      "knowledge_point": {
        "db_id": 17592186087717,
        "id": "bbf50e27-a8c3-52e7-be21-5d7ed61e5512",
        "title": "Filling a Table of Values for a Parametric Curve"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "6b1e8ea8-15aa-5d3b-9214-bdd6c5764764",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/problem": "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{3}\\right),\\qquad y=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{4}\\right).\n$$\n\nConsider the following table of values. Angles are in radians.\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $b$ |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ | $0$ |\n\n| **$t$** | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ |\n| $y$ | $c$ | $a$ |\n\nFind the exact value of $-a+b-c$.\n\n{{result}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The $a$ entry is in the $y$-row under $t=4$. Substitute into $y=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{4}\\right)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a &=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi \\left(4\\right)}{4}\\right) \\\\ &=\\cos\\left(\\pi\\right) \\\\ &=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $b$ entry is in the $x$-row under $t=2$. Substitute into $x=\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{3}\\right)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b &=\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\pi \\left(2\\right)}{3}\\right) \\\\ &=\\tan\\left(\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}\\right) \\\\ &=- \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $c$ entry is in the $y$-row under $t=3$. Substitute into $y=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{4}\\right)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c &=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi \\left(3\\right)}{4}\\right) \\\\ &=\\cos\\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}\\right) \\\\ &=- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute the three entries with the signs in the requested expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}-a+b-c \\\\ =-\\left(-1\\right)+\\left(- \\sqrt{3}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\ =- \\sqrt{3} + \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} + 1\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nThe completed table is\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $- \\sqrt{3}$ |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ | $0$ |\n\n| **$t$** | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ |\n| $y$ | $- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ | $-1$ |",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
